Speaker diarization toolkit

Usage: polyvoice [OPTIONS] [WAV]
       polyvoice <COMMAND>

Commands:
  diarize          Run diarization on a WAV file (same as the bare `polyvoice <wav>` form)
  download-models  Download Mobile/Balanced ONNX models
  models           Inspect models registry
  completions      Generate shell completions to stdout
  schema           Print the JSON Schema of the diarization result to stdout (agent contract)
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [WAV]  WAV file to diarize. `polyvoice meeting.wav` diarizes it directly

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          [default: balanced]
      --output <OUTPUT>
          Write output to a file instead of stdout
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: rttm] [possible values: rttm, json, srt, vtt, txt]
      --models-cache <MODELS_CACHE>
          
      --threshold <THRESHOLD>
          [default: 0.45]
      --speakers <SPEAKERS>
          Target speaker count (caps clustering at N speakers)
      --max-speakers <MAX_SPEAKERS>
          Maximum number of speakers (clustering ceiling)
      --quiet
          Suppress progress/info on stderr
      --json
          Machine mode: emit only the structured JSON result on stdout; route all human-readable output to stderr. Implies `--format json --quiet`
      --v2
          Use pipeline v2 (experimental; not recommended for long-form audio)
      --clusterer <CLUSTERER>
          v2 clusterer: `ahc` (default cosine AHC) or `vbx` (PLDA + VB-HMM — best for overlap-heavy / meeting audio; needs the `vbx` build feature and a PLDA dir via `--vbx-plda-dir` or `POLYVOICE_VBX_PLDA_DIR`). Only affects `--v2` [default: ahc]
      --vbx-plda-dir <VBX_PLDA_DIR>
          Directory with the precomputed VBx PLDA params (overrides `POLYVOICE_VBX_PLDA_DIR`). Only used with `--v2 --clusterer vbx`
      --embed-window <EMBED_WINDOW>
          v2 dense embedding window in seconds (e.g. `1.5`): split segments into overlapping sub-windows for more embeddings per speaker — lower confusion on clean audio at the cost of more embedder calls. Omit for one embedding/segment. Only affects `--v2`
      --execution-provider <EXECUTION_PROVIDER>
          ONNX execution provider: `auto` (CoreML on Apple Silicon, XNNPACK on aarch64 Linux, else CPU), `cpu`, `coreml`, `nnapi`, `cuda`, `xnnpack`. Providers not compiled into this build log a warning and run on CPU. Only affects `--v2`; the legacy default pipeline keeps its built-in per-session defaults [default: auto]
      --exclusive
          Also emit a single-speaker (exclusive) timeline. In JSON this is the additive `exclusive_turns` field beside the overlap-aware `turns`. For RTTM/SRT/VTT/TXT the exclusive timeline is written instead (ASR- reconciliation surface — concurrent speakers are collapsed per frame)
  -h, --help
          Print help
  -V, --version
          Print version
